  "subject": "Catdef plugin packaging brief — Track A of CA-008 (plugin ship to claude-community marketplace); separate repo github.com/catdef/catdef-plugin, MIT, plugin name `catdef`, three bundled skills (/catdef:validate / /catdef:scaffold / /catdef:extract), .mcp.json points at catdef.org/mcp (planned URL; server stands up on its own clock per CA-008 Directive 3); manifest + listing copy + submission flow + open verification questions all attached",

  "sent": "2026-05-25T19:00:00-04:00",
  "action_required": true,

  "body": "Action-required brief to the canonical-implementor seat (status: informal; this memo waits if vacant, same pattern as prior cross-seat memos). **Background:** CA-008 ratified the catdef plugin ship as Track A of the disposition on thingalog-strategist's 2026-05-25T12:00 memo. The plugin packages existing catdef-spec content + three skills + an MCP client config pointing at catdef.org/mcp, ships to the claude-community marketplace, MIT license, plugin name `catdef`. **Why a separate brief and not just an in-CA build directive:** CA-008's plain-text directives cover catdef-maintainer (proposal artifact + governance text) and canonical-implementor (the catdef.org/mcp server build, Directive 3). Plugin packaging is **execution work** — implementer-side, not strategist-side — but the strategic shape (manifest content, listing copy, marketplace targeting, submission flow) was worked through with the Director in the strategist session 2026-05-25 and benefits from being captured as input rather than re-derived by whoever staffs canonical-implementor. **What this memo contains (body_ref):** (1) repo recommendation (separate repo `github.com/catdef/catdef-plugin` ratified by Director); (2) proposed manifest content with all required + recommended fields; (3) the three skills' role descriptions (each needs its own SKILL.md drafted during packaging); (4) `.mcp.json` shape for pointing at catdef.org/mcp; (5) README content sketch; (6) marketplace listing copy (short form + long form, both Director-edited, ready to use verbatim); (7) submission flow per Anthropic's plugin docs at code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins; (8) four open verification questions to resolve before submitting. **What you should do when staffed:** read the body_ref; verify the four open questions (`.mcp.json` remote-MCP schema, plugin loading behavior when MCP URL is unreachable, CI auto-bump behavior, catdef.org DNS commitment); package the plugin per the brief; run `claude plugin validate` locally; submit via claude.ai/settings/plugins/submit; file a status memo back to catdef-strategist when submitted (and again when approved/pinned). **What you should NOT do:** modify the strategic shape (manifest fields, listing copy, marketplace target, skill set) without filing a memo back to catdef-strategist first. Tactical packaging choices (how each SKILL.md is worded, README structure beyond the sketch, version-tag scheme) are within scope; strategic-shape changes require strategist sign-off. **Timing:** PO is initiating the Anthropic-arc per CA-008's strategic context. ~1-2 weeks to shippable is the working estimate. No hard deadline; bounded urgency. **Standing posture:** plugin ship does not block on catdef.org/mcp existing (Directive 3 from CA-008 stands up the server on its own clock); the plugin's `.mcp.json` points at the planned URL and gracefully degrades to skills-only behavior until the server is live.",
  "body_ref": "2026-05-25-1900--catdef-strategist--canonical-implementor--catdef-plugin-packaging-brief.body.md",

